initramfs/prepare-ubuntu and the Ubuntu hand-off in initramfs/init:
  Adapted from initramfs/init-ncm in the same erhai commit (GPL-2.0-only).
  Retains HTTP-to-RAM SquashFS, OverlayFS, switch_root, a temporary USB console,
  and a systemd session-expiry timer. Omits persistent mounts, device-specific
  probes, chunked-download workarounds and background restart loops. The host
  explicitly releases a FIFO after its single-file HTTP service is ready;
  a failed download/hash/mount stops preparation. The expiry timer has no
  default dependencies so ordinary boot jobs cannot postpone its activation.
  An explicit experimental NBD transport uses the existing BusyBox client and
  a read-only QEMU NBD export; it is not the default or an automatic fallback.
  Host SHA verification of a named export is not guest full-image verification.
  Its QEMU handoff passed but the first piano block read failed; HTTP remains
  the device-tested path. No NBD implementation is copied here.
initramfs/ubuntu-state is new GPL-2.0-only read-only session diagnostics.

No stock ROM, device firmware, calibration, keys or device backups are distributed
by this repository. Kernel and other dependencies retain their own licenses.

